1
00:00:00,141 --> 00:00:01,350
Waves breaking over the rail.

2
00:00:02,101 --> 00:00:03,454
Water in the boat past your knees.

3
00:00:04,245 --> 00:00:05,739
Men screaming for their lives.

4
00:00:06,667 --> 00:00:09,205
And in the stern He is asleep.

5
00:00:10,842 --> 00:00:12,495
He is not asleep because He doesn't care.

6
00:00:13,522 --> 00:00:15,555
He is asleep because He has nothing to fear

7
00:00:15,615 --> 00:00:17,095
from the very thing that is killing them.

8
00:00:18,364 --> 00:00:19,954
They shake Him awake, raging that He could

9
00:00:19,994 --> 00:00:20,718
possibly sleep through this.

10
00:00:21,948 --> 00:00:25,937
He opens His eyes: Why are ye fearful, O ye

11
00:00:25,978 --> 00:00:26,782
of little faith?

12
00:00:27,427 --> 00:00:29,480
Then he arose, and rebuked the winds and the

13
00:00:29,540 --> 00:00:31,241
sea; and there was a great calm.

14
00:00:32,203 --> 00:00:34,399
You'll say easy for Him, He's God.

15
00:00:35,252 --> 00:00:35,740
Exactly.

16
00:00:36,329 --> 00:00:37,902
The One who could sleep through it is the One

17
00:00:37,932 --> 00:00:39,165
who silenced it with a word.

18
00:00:39,974 --> 00:00:41,628
You have admired this scene your whole life.

19
00:00:42,136 --> 00:00:43,829
But when the water reaches your knees, you

20
00:00:43,849 --> 00:00:44,625
don't trust the Christ in the boat.

21
00:00:45,882 --> 00:00:48,359
You wake Him, furious, certain He doesn't care.

22
00:00:49,108 --> 00:00:50,501
He doesn't despise little faith.

23
00:00:51,210 --> 00:00:52,986
He grows it by showing you Himself.

24
00:00:53,894 --> 00:00:55,730
Come to the Christ who slept unafraid.

25
00:00:56,597 --> 00:00:59,395
He is asking you why are you afraid?
